    "title": "What's closed on Good Friday? Are banks open today? What to know in Tennessee",
    "text": "What's closed on Good Friday? Are banks open today? What to know in TennesseeMillions of Christians will celebrate Easter Sunday this weekend, which falls on April 5 this year. However, before Easter Sunday comes Good Friday, one of the holiest days of the year in Christianity.Marking the end of Lent — the 40‑day season of prayer, fasting and reflection observed by many Christians, particularly Roman Catholics — Good Friday commemorates the crucifixion of Jesus Christ.Officially established by the fourth century and believed to date back to the era of Jesus’ death, Good Friday has long been observed as a solemn day of remembrance ahead of Easter.Here's what to know about Good Friday, including what's open and closed in Tennessee.When is Good Friday 2026? Why is it observed?Because Good Friday is associated with Easter, its date changes annually. In 2026, the holiday will fall on April 3.In the Christian faith, Good Friday is observed during Holy Week and commemorates the crucifixion of Jesus Christ. The day symbolizes loss, sacrifice and waiting, and is traditionally marked as a time of mourning, when churches become solemn and celebrations pause, according to the Old Farmer's Almanac.On the Christian calendar, Good Friday falls between Maundy Thursday and Holy Saturday and is part of the Easter Triduum — the three sacred days leading up to Easter Sunday.Are Middle Tennessee schools open on Good Friday? See listIn the U.S., whether schools close in observance of Good Friday depends on the school district. Good Friday is recognized as a state holiday in Tennessee, which means many students may have the day off.Below is a list of Nashville-area and surrounding county school closures:Is Good Friday a federal holiday? Are Tennessee government offices open?Good Friday is not a federal holiday, although Tennessee does recognize it as a state holiday, meaning that non-essential government offices will be closed.Other states which also recognize Good Friday include Connecticut, Delaware, Hawaii, Indiana, Kentucky, Louisiana, North Carolina, North Dakota, New Jersey, and Texas, according to Timeanddate.com.Are banks, the stock market open on Good Friday?Since Good Friday is not a federal holiday, most banks in the U.S. will remain open. The stock market, however, will close in observance of the holiday.The bond market will close early, at 1 p.m. CT, according to Investopedia. Both markets will open for business as usual on April 6, the day after Easter.Is mail delivered on Good Friday?The United States Postal Service (USPS) delivers mail on Good Friday as it is not a federal holiday. FedEx and UPS will also operate as normal and locations will be open, according to company holiday schedules.Diana Leyva covers trending news and service journalism for The Tennessean. Contact her at Dleyva@gannett.com.This article originally appeared on Nashville Tennessean: Are banks open today? What is closed on Good Friday in Tennessee",
